**1. A computer-implemented method for decoding a received codeword over a Galois field, the method comprising:**

defining \(GF(2^m)\) using a primitive polynomial \(P(x)\) of degree \(m\) and a primitive element \(\alpha\) that is a root of \(P(x)\);

generating or accessing exponent lookup values that associate respective nonzero field elements of \(GF(2^m)\), represented as \(m\)-bit values, with respective powers of \(\alpha\), with field-element reduction being performed modulo \(P(x)\);

selecting a plurality of the powers of \(\alpha\) as roots of a generator polynomial \(G(x)\);

expanding  
\[
G(x)=\prod_{i\in I}(x-\alpha^i)
\]
over \(GF(2^m)\), using the exponent lookup values to perform at least one field multiplication during the expanding, to obtain coefficients of \(G(x)\);

representing the received codeword as a received polynomial \(C(x)\) having coefficients in \(GF(2^m)\);

performing polynomial division of \(C(x)\) by the expanded generator polynomial \(G(x)\), with coefficient arithmetic performed in \(GF(2^m)\), to obtain a remainder polynomial \(R(x)\) satisfying  
\[
C(x)=Q(x)G(x)+R(x),\qquad \deg R(x)<\deg G(x);
\]
and

decoding the received codeword based at least in part on \(R(x),\) including identifying the received codeword as error-free when \(R(x)=0\) or initiating error-location or error-correction processing when \(R(x)\ne 0\).
